   <system:String x:Key="OpenSeesNonlinearGroup">Nonlinear scheme analysis</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="OpenSeesFiberStatesGroup">Fiber state recording</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="OpenSeesRecordFiberStatesLabel">Record fiber states (σ, ε)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="OpenSeesRecordFiberStatesTip">Writes stress and strain of every fiber of every section at every successful step to nonlinear_fiber_states.out. Gives a detailed fiber-level view on the result tab, but for large models with many steps the file can reach hundreds of MB. Disabling saves disk space and analysis time, but fiber data will no longer be available.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="OpenSeesFiberStatesIntegrationPointsLabel">Integration points to record</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="OpenSeesFiberStatesIntegrationPointsTip">Integration point numbers along the length of each element (1-based, comma-separated, e.g. "1,3,5"). Empty — record all points. Lets you drastically shrink the file by limiting recording to, for example, just the end sections of elements.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CsfeaSettingsGroup">CSfea — secant schema analysis</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CsfeaThreadsLabel">Section update threads (0 — all cores)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CsfeaThreadsTip">How many threads update secant element stiffnesses per iteration. 0 — number of cores; fewer — leave cores to other programs.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="OpenSeesMaterialsGroup">Materials (nonlinear analysis)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsGridGroup">Post-processor</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsGridDensity">Grid density (steps per max(w,h))</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsNewtonGroup">Newton iterations</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsTol">Convergence tolerance, kN</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsMaxIter">Max iterations</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsDeltaH">Numerical derivative step h</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsJacobian">Jacobian scheme</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsJacobianForward">Forward</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsJacobianCentral">Central</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp63EtaMin">SP63 desc. branch: η_min</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp63EtaMinTip">Lower bound of SP63 App.G descending branch. Per SP 63.13330 §G.1 — not less than 0.85</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsEkbEtaMin">CEB-FIP desc. branch: η_min</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsEkbEtaMinTip">Lower bound of the CEB-FIP (EKB) descending branch (η = σ/Rb). The MC90 eq. (2.1-20) branch starts at η = 0.5, so it is not built when η ≥ 0.5. Default 0.05</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsShellTolRes">Tolerance (plates)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsShellTolResTip">Relative Newton tolerance for plate sections: ‖residual‖ / (1 + ‖target forces‖). Recommended: 1e-3.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsLimitBisectGroup">Limit forces: bisection on k</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsLimitBisectAbs">Absolute tolerance on k</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsLimitBisectRel">Relative tolerance on k (fraction of k)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsLimitBisectTip">Bisection on the load factor k stops when the interval width does not exceed the smaller of the two tolerances: absolute and relative·k. Relative 0 — absolute only. The force residual at each trial point is the Newton tolerance above, a separate quantity. Defaults 1e-4 and 1e-5.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="PlotSettingsForceSetColorize">Colorize force values in sets by axis</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="PlotSettingsForceSetColorizeTip">When enabled, force set table values are colored like the sign convention card: N/T — red, Mx/Vx/Qx/Nx — green, My/Vy/Qy/Ny — blue; Nxy — dark red, Mxy — orange.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsRcGroup">RC cross-section</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsRebarDifferentialDiagram">Account for concrete area reduction replaced by rebar</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsRebarCompressionByRs">Compressed rebar in the strain method — by Rs (legacy)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsRebarCompressionByRsTip">Fallback mode. By default the compression branch of bilinear and trilinear rebar diagrams follows the tension branch and is capped at the design compressive resistance Rsc (SP 63.13330 cl. 6.2.13). When enabled, compression is symmetric to tension — up to Rs (1.1·Rs for the trilinear diagram), as in OpenCS before 22.10.2026. Formula checks and custom diagrams are not affected.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsRebarDifferentialDiagramTip">When enabled, rebar in concrete accounts for concrete area displaced by the bar (differential diagram σ_st − σ_bc). When disabled, the pure steel diagram is used and the concrete mesh includes the bar footprint.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsPsiSMethod">ψs coefficient method (crack width)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsPsiSMethodStress">§8.2.18 — stress ratio</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsPsiSMethodStrain">§8.2.32 — strain ratio</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsPsiSMethodTip">How ψs (non-uniform strain distribution of tensioned rebar between cracks) is computed in crack-width tasks: from the stress ratio σs,crc/σs (formula 8.138, §8.2.18 — the standard approach) or from the strain ratio εs,crc/εs (deformation-model formula, §8.2.32). For elastic rebar the strain-based variant gives a slightly larger ψs (and hence crack width) under the same loading.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsConsiderConcreteTensionUls">Account for concrete tension in ULS (limit state 1) checks</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsElasticStiffnessWithoutRebar">Baseline elastic stiffness excludes rebar</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsElasticStiffnessWithoutRebarTip">Baseline (EA, EI) used to normalize the stiffness reduction factors of the moment-curvature task. When enabled, the baseline is the bare elastic concrete section without rebar — it then matches the linear member stiffness of an elastic FEA model, where rebar is not modelled, so the factors transfer directly. When disabled, the baseline is the transformed concrete + rebar section.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsConsiderConcreteTensionUlsTip">Affects limit-force and strain-plane search for CalcType C/CL — for both bar and plate sections. Does not affect SLS (N/NL). For plates, overrides the section page's "Concrete tension" flag only in this mode.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsFireCompressionZoneMethod">Compression zone depth for thermal curvature</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsFireCompressionZoneMethodTip">SP 468 formula (8.11) applies to rectangular, T- and I-sections; for an arbitrary outline the fire fiber section equilibrium is used. In "Automatic" mode formula (8.11) is tried first.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsFireCompressionZone_Auto">Automatic</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsFireCompressionZone_Formula">SP 468 formula (8.11)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsFireCompressionZone_Fiber">Fiber section equilibrium</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="FireCurvature_WidthUndefined">The section web width is undefined - formula (8.11) is not applicable.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="FireCurvature_H0Undefined">The effective depth of the section is undefined.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="FireCurvature_ConcreteUndefined">Concrete is not defined in the fire fiber section.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsBatchGroup">Batch Tasks</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsShearInclinedGroup">Inclined Sections (SP 63, 8.1.32–8.1.35)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsShearMomentZoneTip">Support zone length for check (8.63); 0 — code value 2·h0 is used</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsShearAnchorageTip">Longitudinal reinforcement engagement factor k; anchorage per 10.3.21–10.3.28 is not verified</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp20Group">SP20 combinations (default γf)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp20GammaG">G — permanent (unfav.)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp20GammaGFav">G — reduced weight (cl. 7.3)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp20GammaL">L — long-term</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp20GammaQ">Q — short-term</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp20GammaA">A — accidental</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="CalcSettingsSp20GammaTip">Used in SP20 combinatorics when γf is not set explicitly in the force set</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="BatchParallel_Label">Parallel execution (clone section per thread)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="BatchParallel_Tip">Recommended for force sets with 50+ rows. Applies to all strength/stiffness batch tasks. Fire-resistance tasks are not affected.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="ShellWarmStart_Label">Shell warm-start (row N result → row N+1 initial guess)</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="ShellWarmStart_Tip">Passes the converged strain state of the previous row as the initial guess for the next. Can speed up uniform force sets but may hurt convergence when Nxy changes sign between rows. Off by default — each row starts from the elastic guess independently.</system:String>
