    <system:String x:Key="FemBucklingForcesGoverning">governing combination of the element (cl. 10.3.2)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemBucklingForcesTip">Envelope — one stability problem: every bar takes its largest compression over all combinations at once, a bar in tension in all of them — its smallest tension. Columns unloaded in one combination do not brace columns loaded in another — conservative. Governing combination — a problem per combination with the largest compression of the element, μ is applied to all combinations (SP 16 cl. 10.3.2); with partial loading and supporting columns μ may be underestimated for full loading. Shells in the envelope problem follow the combination governing for most elements.</system:String>
