    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPhysicalNonlinearityLabel">Physical nonlinearity</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPhysicalNonlinearityTip">Unchecked — sections are elastic (gross concrete, as in the linear analysis): stepped analysis with geometric nonlinearity only. Cracking, ψs and stirrup shear settings have no effect.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemAnalysisKindTip">The primary solver is our own (CSfea): secant analysis with CScore sections, cracking, ψs and reinforcement yielding, and linear analysis of independent load cases with a single factorization. OpenSees is a fallback.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaStagesHint">A stage applies the load × "Max λ" in round(max / step) steps on top of the state of previous stages.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPlateRebarSourceLabel">Plate reinforcement</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPlateRebarSourceTip">Reinforcement source for plate elements — as in the FE check. Elements without reinforcement are elastic.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaRebarSourceAssigned">Assigned (LIRA)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaRebarSourceSelected">Designed (LIRA ASP)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTensionConcreteLabel">Concrete in tension</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTensionConcreteTip">Tensile work of concrete before cracking. "As in section" — per the plate section setting; bars — with tension.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTensionInherit">As in section</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTensionYes">Yes</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTensionNo">No</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPlateCrackRuleLabel">Plate cracking</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPlateCrackRuleTip">Per layer — only the cracked layer loses tension. Cracked section — the first crack switches off tensile concrete of the whole section (as the bar NDM per SP 63 cl. 8.2.32); tension stiffening comes from ψs only.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaCrackRuleLayer">Per layer</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaCrackRuleSection">Cracked section</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPoissonUncrackedLabel">Uncracked concrete ν</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPoissonUncrackedTip">Poisson ratio of concrete before cracking (0 ≤ ν &lt; 0.5). Empty — as in section.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPoissonInvalid">Uncracked concrete ν must be a number from 0 to 0.5 (exclusive) or empty.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPsiLabel">ψs at cracks (cl. 8.2.32)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaPsiTip">Coefficient ψs of non-uniform strain of tensile reinforcement between cracks (SP 63 cl. 8.2.32).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaBeamShearLabel">Bar shear from stirrups</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaBeamShearTip">Shear deformations of bars (Timoshenko elements): secant GAv from the section stirrups.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaImportedFactorsLabel">Imported stiffness reduction factors</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaImportedFactorsTip">Factors to the initial elastic concrete stiffness set in the imported LIRA model: plate PLKE and WLKE, bar EIy/EIz. Used in the linear analysis and in the secant one without physical nonlinearity; SCAD models carry no such factors.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaGeomNonlinearLabel">Geometric nonlinearity</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaGeomNonlinearTip">Second-order analysis (deformed configuration): the initial stress matrix from the forces of the previous iteration is added to the secant stiffness — P-Δ of bars, walls and plates. A matrix that is no longer positive definite means loss of stability. Large displacements — separate option.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaShellInPlanePDeltaLabel">Account for in-plane deflection of walls and plates</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaShellInPlanePDeltaTip">On: P-Δ of walls and plates both out of plane and in plane (a wall or pier compressed and bent in its plane). Off: out-of-plane deflection only.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaLocalPDeltaLabel">P-δ only (no storey sway)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaLocalPDeltaTip">Second-order theory for local bending of columns and walls between floors only: K_σ of vertical elements uses displacements without the rigid sway of the segment between levels (floors, end cuts); horizontal elements get no K_σ. Intended for a fragment on masks of a linear parent; acceptable when the frame is not sway-sensitive (parent λ_cr ≥ 10). Not with "Large displacements".</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaFragmentSecondOrderLabel">Fragment second order even on first-order masks (no η)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaFragmentSecondOrderTip">Fragment: force sets of an analysis with geometric nonlinearity are treated as second order (η is not applied in the FE check) even if the masks come from a first-order parent (linear CSfea without P-Δ, secant without geometric nonlinearity, SCAD, LIRA-SAPR). The storey sway is then not amplified — the user's decision. Without the flag such sets are first order (η is applied). Bottom/top end cuts must still take displacements from the masks.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaLargeDisplacementsLabel">Large displacements</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaLargeDisplacementsTip">Corotational formulation of plates and bars: large rotations, equilibrium by Newton iterations at every iteration. Noticeably slower; rarely needed — flexible systems, snap-through. Off: second-order analysis.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaIterationsGroup">Iterations (Picard)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaMaxIterationsLabel">Max iterations per step</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaMaxIterationsInvalid">Number of iterations must be an integer ≥ 1.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaMaxBisectionsLabel">Step bisections</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaMaxBisectionsTip">How many times a non-converged step is halved before the stage is considered a limit stage.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaMaxBisectionsInvalid">Number of bisections must be an integer ≥ 0.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTolDisplacementLabel">Tolerance ‖Δu‖/‖u‖</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTolStiffnessLabel">Stiffness tolerance</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaTolStiffnessTip">Tolerance of the secant stiffness change between iterations (work measure).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaToleranceInvalid">Tolerances must be positive numbers.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaOmega0Label">Relaxation ω₀</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaOmega0Tip">Initial relaxation factor of secant stiffnesses (0 &lt; ω₀ ≤ 1).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaOmega0Invalid">Relaxation ω₀ must be in (0; 1].</system:String>
