    <system:String x:Key="MosaicStiffnessModeTip">Element stiffness: E₀ — initial, E — secant (state of the shown step), E/E₀ — their ratio. Plates — in force output axes: when the output axis is at an angle to the reinforcement, E1, E2, G are the diagonal of the rotated matrix, not orthotropic moduli. Bars — at points i, ½, j.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="CsfeaBarStiffnessAggregateLabel">Bar stiffness mosaic — element value</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="CsfeaBarStiffnessAggregateTip">How a bar element is coloured in the CSfea stiffness mosaic (diagrams off): by the minimum of the values at points i, ½, j or by the mean along the bar (Simpson over three points).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="CsfeaStiffnessFloorLabel">Stiffness lower bound e_min (linear on secant)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="CsfeaStiffnessFloorTip">CSfea linear analysis on the stiffnesses of a secant result (engineering nonlinearity): the element section matrix diagonal is at least e_min of the initial elastic one. Default 0.01; 0 &lt; e_min &lt; 1.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaStiffnessGroup">Element stiffnesses</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCsfeaStiffnessTip">Engineering nonlinearity: linear analysis of load cases on the secant stiffnesses of the final state of a secant analysis of the model. The governing combination is reproduced exactly, others approximately (cracks come from the governing loading).</system:String>
