    <system:String x:Key="FemAnalysisConsiderPhysicalNonlinearityTip">When disabled, the section is built not from fibers but as a single linear-elastic section (section Elastic) with transformed EA/EIz/EIy relative to the elastic modulus of the material with the largest area — materials and fibers are absent from the model entirely, and CScore diagrams are never requested. Geometric nonlinearity (P-Δ/large displacement) keeps working as configured. Useful to isolate geometric effects from material ones during debugging/verification, or for a quick linear-elastic run with large displacements.</system:String>
