    <system:String x:Key="Sp16MeshLef">lef = μ·l, l from the schema mesh for each element</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Sp16MeshLefHint">l is the length of the chain of collinear bars between nodes where other elements join. One l for both planes; a joint is not necessarily an out-of-plane restraint (bracing, purlins) — account for it via μ. Elements of SCAD steel groups take lengths from their groups. Unchecked — lef,x and lef,y from the group SP 16 parameters.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Sp16MeshMuB">μb for φb: beam lef = μb·l; 0 — beam lef from the group SP 16 parameters</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Sp16MeshMuBShort">μb</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="FemCheckDlgSteelLef">Effective lengths</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="Sp16AutoLef">Auto (FEM): μ from the stability analysis of the model</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="Sp16AutoLefHint">Before the check a linear buckling analysis of the undeformed model is solved (SP 16 cl. 10.3.11): elastic sections, combinations are the stages of the selected analysis, each element (structural member or chain of FEs) uses the combination with the largest compression (cl. 10.3.2). μ = π/l·√(EI/N_cr), N_cr = λ·N of the lowest mode the element takes part in; a leaning element gets μ = 1. Where μ is not assigned (element not in the modes, model unstable) lengths come from the mesh or the SP 16 parameters. Elements of SCAD steel groups take lengths from their groups.</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="Sp16AutoLefAnalysis">Analysis:</system:String>
   <system:String x:Key="Sp16AutoLefAnalysisHint">An “Effective lengths — CSfea” analysis (recommended): μ are taken from its saved result; when the model, loads or combinations change it is recomputed and saved. An analysis of another kind: its stages are the combinations, the buckling analysis runs before every check and is not saved.</system:String>
